Backport of upstream llama.cpp commit
    d0a6dfeb28a09831d904fc4d910ddb740da82834
    "ggml-webgpu: Add the support of `MUL_MAT_ID` (#21147)"
    https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/21147
    2026-04-06, Masashi Yoshimura, co-authored by Reese Levine

GGML_OP_MUL_MAT_ID is the MoE expert FFN. Without it ggml-webgpu falls to the
`default` arm of supports_op and reports every MoE model as unexecutable, which
is what kept Qwen3.6-35B-A3B out of reach (docs/CONSTRAINTS.md F14).

Backport rather than a fork update: the fork llmlet pins (ktock/llama.cpp
c4b18b39d) sits on upstream f49e9178, 40 commits before this one. Upstream
master is 2012 commits further on and would put patches/0001-0003 - the O9 fix
in particular - back under test for no gain here.

Files, taken from upstream unchanged except where noted:
    ggml/src/ggml-webgpu/ggml-webgpu.cpp                     (encode path,
        get_alloc_size for the gather buffers, and the supports_op case)
    ggml/src/ggml-webgpu/ggml-webgpu-shader-lib.hpp          (shader variants)
    ggml/src/ggml-webgpu/wgsl-shaders/mul_mat_decls.tmpl
    ggml/src/ggml-webgpu/wgsl-shaders/mul_mat_id.wgsl        (new)
    ggml/src/ggml-webgpu/wgsl-shaders/mul_mat_id_gather.wgsl (new)

The one adaptation, in ggml-webgpu.cpp only. Of the 40 commits between the pin
and this one, exactly one touched this file: d00685831 ("ggml-webgpu: move from
parameter buffer pool to single buffer with offsets", #21278). It changed how
every op submits work, so upstream's ggml_webgpu_mul_mat_id() is written
against the newer convention and does not apply here. It is reworded to the
pinned one, and nothing else:

    webgpu_encoded_op                      -> webgpu_command
    wgpu::CommandEncoder & encoder param   -> dropped
    ctx->param_arena                       -> ctx->param_buf_pool

The pin already has ggml_backend_webgpu_build_multi() with the same shape minus
the encoder, and already dispatches several pipelines for one op through it
(see ggml_webgpu_argsort), so this is a call-convention rewording and not a
reimplementation. The shaders and the shader-lib entries are byte-for-byte
upstream. Line counts match the upstream commit exactly: +585/-1 across the
five files.

d00685831 itself is deliberately not taken: it rewrites the submission path of
every op in the file (+557/-403) and overlaps the region patches/0003 depends
on, which is a much larger blast radius than this phase can justify.

Also deliberately not taken:
    a95a11e5b (#22464) mat-vec/mat-mat performance for MUL_MAT_ID - this phase
        does no performance work.
    20d3bc2cc (#21872) shader-lib dequantisation refactor - unrelated cleanup
        written against a later shader-lib than the pin has.
    docs/ops.md and docs/ops/WebGPU.csv from the upstream commit - op-coverage
        documentation, no effect on behaviour.

Accepted src0 types are F32/F16/Q4_0/Q4_1/Q5_0/Q5_1/Q8_0/Q2_K/Q3_K/Q4_K/Q5_K/
Q6_K. There is no IQ support, so a model whose expert tensors are IQ-quantised
still cannot run on a WebGPU peer; scripts/probe-gguf-header.mjs reports that
per model.

